module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smoothing.PositiveCharacteristicResolution

/-!
# Resolving the twisted quotient chain of Stacks 07FJ

The proof of Stacks 07FJ is a twenty-six item argument. Items (1)–(18) are carried out in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smoothing.PositiveCharacteristicResolution`, which reduces 07FJ to
`Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientResolvable`: the chain produced by item (18) (Stacks 07G2),

`R/I → (R ⊗_{k[x_1, …, x_d]} C)/I → Λ/IΛ ⊃ 𝔮/IΛ`,

can be resolved, where `R = k[y_1, …, y_m, t_1, …, t_d]` carries `x_i ↦ γ_i = π_i t_i` and
`I = (γ_1^e, …, γ_d^e)` with `e = 8c`. Items (19) and (21) of the source only introduce notation
(the primes `𝔯 ⊂ R` and the ideal `J = (π_1^e, …, π_d^e)`), so the mathematical content of the
remainder is items (20) and (22)–(26).

This file carries out item (20) — Stacks 07G4: the reduction of the twisted quotient chain to
its localization at `𝔮`. The point is that dividing by `I` makes the localized target
zero-dimensional. Indeed `IΛ` is generated by the elements `(δ_iφ(π_i))^e`, the `δ_i` are units
in `Λ_𝔮`, the `φ(π_i)` generate the maximal ideal of `Λ_𝔮`, and `n > d(e - 1)` — which is the
corrected bound of item (7) recorded in `TwistedQuotientResolvable` — so

`𝔮^nΛ_𝔮 ⊆ IΛ_𝔮`.

Hence `𝔮` is minimal over `IΛ`, the prime `𝔮/IΛ` is a minimal prime of `Λ/IΛ`, and the maximal
ideal of `(Λ/IΛ)_{𝔮/IΛ}` is generated by the nilpotent images of the `φ(π_i)`. That is exactly
the input of `Stacks.Smoothing.LocalSmoothingSituation.canBeResolved_of_nilpotent_generators`,
which is Stacks 07G4 and in turn Stacks 07FA.

What is *not* done here are items (22)–(26), i.e. Stacks 07G6, 07G7, 07G8, 07G9 and 07GA: the
passage from the localized chain over `(R/I)_𝔯` to the chain over `(R/𝔭^nR)_𝔭`, the replacement
of `C` by `B`, and the factorization through `D'[t_1, …, t_d]`. They are carried as the single
named hypothesis `Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable`, which is
`TwistedQuotientResolvable` on the same data with `CanBeResolved` weakened to
`Stacks.Smoothing.LocalSmoothingSituation.IsResolvableAfterLocalizing` — the conclusion asked
for only after localizing at `𝔮`, which is the form in which the source's items (22)–(26)
establish it.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable`: items (22)–(26) of the proof of Stacks
  07FJ — the twisted quotient chain of item (18) is resolvable after localizing at `𝔮`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Smoothing.canBeResolved_quotient_of_isResolvableAfterLocalizing`: Stacks 07G4 for a
  chain divided by an ideal whose extension to the target is generated by the `e`-th powers of a
  regular system of parameters scaled by units.
* `Stacks.Smoothing.twistedQuotientResolvable_of_locallyResolvable`:
  `TwistedQuotientResolvable` from `TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable`.
* `Stacks.Smoothing.canBeResolvedInPositiveCharacteristic_of_locallyResolvable`: the current
  state of Stacks 07FJ — proved from exactly two undischarged hypotheses,
  `Stacks.Smoothing.HasArtinianApproximationData` (item (9), Stacks 07FT) and
  `Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable` (items (22)–(26), Stacks 07G6–07GA).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07FJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07FJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07G4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07G4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Stacks.Smoothing

universe u

/-! ### A prime minimal over a product of unit multiples of parameter powers -/

section ParameterPowers

variable {Λ : Type u} [CommRing Λ]

/-- The extension to `Λ_𝔮` of the ideal generated by the `e`-th powers of the `δ_iρ_i` is the
ideal generated by the `e`-th powers of the `ρ_i`, because the `δ_i` become units. -/
theorem map_span_mul_pow_eq (q : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] {d e : ℕ} (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hδ : ∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl) :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q))
        (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i) ^ e) := by
  have hinv : ∀ i, ∃ v : Localization.AtPrime q,
      v * algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (δ i) = 1 := fun i =>
    (IsLocalization.map_units (Localization.AtPrime q) (⟨δ i, hδ i⟩ : q.primeCompl)).exists_left_inv
  have hle : ∀ f g : Fin d → Localization.AtPrime q, (∀ i, ∃ c, f i = c * g i) →
      Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range g) := fun f g h => by
    rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h i
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, hc]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  refine le_antisymm (hle _ _ fun i => ⟨algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (δ i) ^ e, ?_⟩)
    (hle _ _ fun i => ?_)
  · simp only [Function.comp_apply, map_pow, map_mul, mul_pow]
  · obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hinv i
    exact ⟨v ^ e, by
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, map_pow, map_mul, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_pow, hv, one_mul]⟩

/-- The `n`-th power of the maximal ideal of `Λ_𝔮` lies in the extension of
`J = ((δ_1ρ_1)^e, …, (δ_dρ_d)^e)`, as soon as `d(e - 1) < n`, when the `ρ_i` generate the maximal
ideal and the `δ_i` are units. This is the numerical heart of item (20): it is what makes the
localized target of the twisted quotient chain zero-dimensional. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_span (q : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] {d e n : ℕ} (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hδ : ∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i)) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q))
    (he : 1 ≤ e) (hne : d * (e - 1) + 1 ≤ n) :
    maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) ^ n ≤
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q))
        (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e)) := by
  rw [map_span_mul_pow_eq q ρ δ hδ, ← hspan]
  exact span_range_pow_le_span_range_pow_of_le _ he hne

/-- The ideal generated by the `e`-th powers of the `δ_iρ_i` lies in `𝔮` when the `ρ_i` do. -/
theorem span_mul_pow_le (q : Ideal Λ) {d e : ℕ} (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ) (hρ : ∀ i, ρ i ∈ q)
    (he : 1 ≤ e) {J : Ideal Λ} (hJ : J = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e)) :
    J ≤ q := by
  rw [hJ, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨i, rfl⟩
  exact q.pow_mem_of_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (hρ i)) e (by omega)

/-- **`𝔮` is minimal over `J`.** If the `ρ_i` generate the maximal ideal of `Λ_𝔮`, the `δ_i` are
units there, `J = ((δ_1ρ_1)^e, …, (δ_dρ_d)^e)` and `d(e - 1) < n`, then no prime strictly inside
`𝔮` contains `J`. -/
theorem le_of_isPrime_of_le (q : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] {d e n : ℕ} (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hδ : ∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i)) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q))
    (he : 1 ≤ e) (hne : d * (e - 1) + 1 ≤ n) {J : Ideal Λ}
    (hJ : J = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e)) (p : Ideal Λ) [hp : p.IsPrime]
    (hJp : J ≤ p) (hpq : p ≤ q) : q ≤ p := by
  intro x hx
  have hdisj : Disjoint (q.primeCompl : Set Λ) (p : Set Λ) := by
    rw [Set.disjoint_left]
    exact fun s hs hsp => hs (hpq hsp)
  have hmem : algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) x ∈ maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
    rw [← IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal q (Localization.AtPrime q)]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hx
  have hpow : algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (x ^ n) ∈
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)) p := by
    rw [map_pow]
    refine Ideal.map_mono (hJ ▸ hJp) (maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_span q ρ δ hδ hspan he hne ?_)
    exact Ideal.pow_mem_pow hmem n
  have hxp : x ^ n ∈ p := by
    have hcomap := IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint q.primeCompl
      (Localization.AtPrime q) hp hdisj
    have hmem' : x ^ n ∈ (Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)) p).under Λ := hpow
    rwa [hcomap] at hmem'
  exact hp.mem_of_pow_mem n hxp

end ParameterPowers

/-! ### The prime of the quotient and its local ring -/

section Quotient

variable {Λ : Type u} [CommRing Λ]

/-- An ideal containing `J` is recovered from its image in `Λ/J`. -/
theorem comap_map_quotient (q J : Ideal Λ) (hJq : J ≤ q) :
    Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q) = q := by
  rw [Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective,
    ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, Ideal.mk_ker, sup_eq_left]
  exact hJq

/-- The image of a prime containing `J` is a prime of `Λ/J`. -/
theorem isPrime_map_quotient (q J : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] (hJq : J ≤ q) :
    (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime :=
  Ideal.map_isPrime_of_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (by rwa [Ideal.mk_ker])

/-- The composite `Λ → Λ/J → (Λ/J)_{𝔮/J}`. -/
noncomputable def toLocQuot (q J : Ideal Λ) [(Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime] :
    Λ →+* Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q) :=
  (algebraMap (Λ ⧸ J) (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q))).comp
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)

/-- Everything outside `𝔮` becomes invertible in `(Λ/J)_{𝔮/J}`. -/
theorem isUnit_toLocQuot (q J : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime]
    [(Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime] (hJq : J ≤ q) (y : q.primeCompl) :
    IsUnit (toLocQuot q J (y : Λ)) := by
  have hy : Ideal.Quotient.mk J (y : Λ) ∈ (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).primeCompl := by
    intro hmem
    refine y.2 ?_
    have hc : (y : Λ) ∈
      Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q) := hmem
    rwa [comap_map_quotient q J hJq] at hc
  exact IsLocalization.map_units _
    (⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk J (y : Λ), hy⟩ : (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).primeCompl)

/-- The maximal ideal of `(Λ/J)_{𝔮/J}` is the image of `𝔮`. -/
theorem map_toLocQuot_eq_maximalIdeal (q J : Ideal Λ)
    [(Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime] :
    Ideal.map (toLocQuot q J) q =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q)) := by
  rw [toLocQuot, ← Ideal.map_map,
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q)
      (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q))]

/-- A ring map out of `Λ` inverting everything outside `𝔮` factors through `Λ_𝔮`, so it carries
generators of the maximal ideal of `Λ_𝔮` to generators of the image of `𝔮`. -/
theorem map_eq_span_of_isUnit (q : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] {L : Type u} [CommRing L] (f : Λ →+* L)
    (hf : ∀ y : q.primeCompl, IsUnit (f (y : Λ))) {d : ℕ} (ρ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i)) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
    Ideal.map f q = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => f (ρ i)) := by
  have hgcomp : (IsLocalization.lift (M := q.primeCompl) (S := Localization.AtPrime q) hf).comp
      (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)) = f :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => IsLocalization.lift_eq hf x
  rw [← hgcomp, ← Ideal.map_map,
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal q (Localization.AtPrime q), ← hspan,
    Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-- The maximal ideal of `(Λ/J)_{𝔮/J}` is generated by the images of the `ρ_i`. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_eq_span_toLocQuot (q J : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime]
    [(Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime] (hJq : J ≤ q) {d : ℕ} (ρ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i)) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
    maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => toLocQuot q J (ρ i)) := by
  rw [← map_toLocQuot_eq_maximalIdeal q J]
  exact map_eq_span_of_isUnit q (toLocQuot q J) (isUnit_toLocQuot q J hJq) ρ hspan

/-- Each generator of the maximal ideal of `(Λ/J)_{𝔮/J}` is nilpotent: the `e`-th power of
`δ_iρ_i` is killed in `Λ/J` and `δ_i` is invertible. -/
theorem isNilpotent_toLocQuot (q J : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime]
    [(Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime] (hJq : J ≤ q) {d e : ℕ} (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hδ : ∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl)
    (hJ : J = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e)) (i : Fin d) :
    IsNilpotent (toLocQuot q J (ρ i)) := by
  refine ⟨e, ?_⟩
  have hzero : toLocQuot q J ((δ i * ρ i) ^ e) = 0 := by
    have hmemJ : (δ i * ρ i) ^ e ∈ J := hJ ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
    rw [toLocQuot]
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hmemJ, map_zero]
  have hu : IsUnit (toLocQuot q J (δ i) ^ e) :=
    (isUnit_toLocQuot q J hJq (⟨δ i, hδ i⟩ : q.primeCompl)).pow e
  rw [map_pow, map_mul, mul_pow] at hzero
  exact hu.mul_left_cancel (by rw [hzero, mul_zero])

/-- **`𝔮/J` is a minimal prime of `Λ/J`.** -/
theorem le_of_isPrime_le_map_quotient (q J : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] (hJq : J ≤ q) {d e n : ℕ}
    (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ) (hδ : ∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i)) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q))
    (he : 1 ≤ e) (hne : d * (e - 1) + 1 ≤ n)
    (hJ : J = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e)) (p : Ideal (Λ ⧸ J))
    (hp : p.IsPrime) (hpq : p ≤ Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q) :
    Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q ≤ p := by
  have hcp : (Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) p).IsPrime := hp.comap _
  have hJle : J ≤ Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) p :=
    Ideal.mk_ker.ge.trans (Ideal.ker_le_comap _)
  have hple : Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) p ≤ q := by
    rw [← comap_map_quotient q J hJq]
    exact Ideal.comap_mono hpq
  exact (Ideal.map_mono (le_of_isPrime_of_le q ρ δ hδ hspan he hne hJ _ hJle hple)).trans_eq
    (Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective p)

end Quotient

/-! ### The extension of the parameter-power ideal to the target -/

/-- The extension to `Λ` of `I = (γ_1^e, …, γ_d^e)` along `R → T → Λ` is generated by the `e`-th
powers of the images `δ_iρ_i` of the `γ_i`. -/
theorem map_map_span_pow_eq {R T Λ : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [CommRing Λ]
    (fRT : R →+* T) (fTΛ : T →+* Λ) {d e : ℕ} (γ : Fin d → R) (δ ρ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hγ : ∀ i, fTΛ (fRT (γ i)) = δ i * ρ i) {I : Ideal R} {ID : Ideal T} {IΛ : Ideal Λ}
    (hI : I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => γ i ^ e)) (hID : ID = Ideal.map fRT I)
    (hIΛ : IΛ = Ideal.map fTΛ ID) :
    IΛ = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e) := by
  rw [hIΛ, hID, hI, Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  refine congrArg Ideal.span (congrArg Set.range (funext fun i => ?_))
  change fTΛ (fRT (γ i ^ e)) = (δ i * ρ i) ^ e
  rw [map_pow, map_pow, hγ i]

/-- The extension to `Λ` of `I = (γ_1^e, …, γ_d^e)` lies in `𝔮` when the images of the `γ_i`
are unit multiples of elements of `𝔮`. -/
theorem map_map_span_pow_le {R T Λ : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [CommRing Λ]
    (fRT : R →+* T) (fTΛ : T →+* Λ) (q : Ideal Λ) {d e : ℕ} (γ : Fin d → R) (δ ρ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hγ : ∀ i, fTΛ (fRT (γ i)) = δ i * ρ i) (hρ : ∀ i, ρ i ∈ q) (he : 1 ≤ e)
    {I : Ideal R} {ID : Ideal T} {IΛ : Ideal Λ}
    (hI : I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => γ i ^ e)) (hID : ID = Ideal.map fRT I)
    (hIΛ : IΛ = Ideal.map fTΛ ID) : IΛ ≤ q :=
  span_mul_pow_le q ρ δ hρ he (map_map_span_pow_eq fRT fTΛ γ δ ρ hγ hI hID hIΛ)

/-- A product with the image of `1` under a ring map. This is the shape in which the composite
`R → R ⊗_S C → L` of the maps lifted from `R → L` and `C → L` evaluates: definitionally it is
the value of `R → L` times the value of `C → L` at `1`. -/
theorem mul_map_one_eq {A L : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing L] (F : A →+* L) (x : L) {y : L}
    (h : x = y) : x * F 1 = y := by
  rw [map_one, mul_one, h]

/-- The value of the twisted structure map `R = k[y_1, …, y_m, t_1, …, t_d] → Λ` on the twisted
parameter `γ_i = π_i t_i` is `δ_i φ(π_i)`. -/
theorem twistedBaseToTarget_twistedParameter {k Λ : Type u} [CommRing k] [CommRing Λ]
    [Algebra k Λ] {m d : ℕ} (φ : MvPolynomial (Fin m) k →ₐ[k] Λ)
    (π : Fin d → MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (δ : Fin d → Λ) (i : Fin d) :
    twistedBaseToTarget φ δ (twistedParameter π i) = δ i * φ (π i) := by
  rw [twistedParameter, map_mul, twistedBaseToTarget_X_inr, mul_comm]
  congr 1
  exact AlgHom.congr_fun (twistedBaseToTarget_comp_rename φ δ) (π i)

/-! ### Two generalities on chains -/

/-- A chain whose own `𝔥_A` is not contained in `𝔮` can be resolved by itself. -/
theorem canBeResolved_of_not_le {R A Λ : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing Λ]
    [Algebra R A] [Algebra A Λ] [Algebra R Λ] [IsScalarTower R A Λ]
    [Algebra.FinitePresentation R A] (q : Ideal Λ)
    (h : ¬ (Ideal.map (algebraMap A Λ) (singularIdeal R A)).radical ≤ q) :
    CanBeResolved R A Λ q :=
  ⟨A, inferInstance, inferInstance, Algebra.id A, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    inferInstance, inferInstance, le_rfl, h⟩

/-- Dividing a chain `R → T` of finite type over a Noetherian base by an ideal of the base and
its extension leaves an algebra of finite presentation. -/
theorem finitePresentation_quotient {R T : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing T]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [Algebra R T] [Algebra.FiniteType R T] (I : Ideal R) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation (R ⧸ I) (T ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R T) I) := by
  have : Algebra.FiniteType R (T ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R T) I) :=
    .of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  exact (Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType (R := R ⧸ I)
    (A := T ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R T) I)).mp
    (Algebra.FiniteType.of_restrictScalars_finiteType R (R ⧸ I) _)

/-! ### Item (20) of the proof of Stacks 07FJ -/

/-- **Stacks 07FJ, item (20)** (tag 07G4) for the twisted quotient chain. Let `R → T → Λ ⊃ 𝔮` be a
chain, let `γ_1, …, γ_d ∈ R` map to `δ_iρ_i` in `Λ` with the `δ_i` units of `Λ_𝔮` and the `ρ_i`
generating the maximal ideal of `Λ_𝔮`, and divide the chain by `I = (γ_1^e, …, γ_d^e)`. If
`d(e - 1) < n`, then the quotient chain can be resolved as soon as it can be resolved after
localizing at `𝔮`.

The hypothesis `hres` is the localized resolvability of the quotient chain; the content proved
here is that the quotient chain satisfies the two remaining hypotheses of Stacks 07FA, namely
that `𝔮/IΛ` is minimal over `𝔥` and that the local ring of `Λ/IΛ` at it is zero-dimensional.
The latter is where the corrected bound of item (7) is used: the maximal ideal of the
localization is generated by the images of the `ρ_i`, and these are nilpotent because
`(δ_iρ_i)^e ∈ IΛ`. -/
theorem canBeResolved_quotient_of_isResolvableAfterLocalizing {Rb Ab Λ : Type u} [CommRing Rb]
    [CommRing Ab] [CommRing Λ] (q : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime] (J : Ideal Λ) [Algebra Rb Ab]
    [Algebra Ab (Λ ⧸ J)] {instRbΛ : Algebra Rb (Λ ⧸ J)}
    {tw : @IsScalarTower Rb Ab (Λ ⧸ J) Algebra.toSMul Algebra.toSMul instRbΛ.toSMul}
    [IsNoetherianRing Rb] (hJq : J ≤ q) {d e n : ℕ} (ρ δ : Fin d → Λ)
    (hδ : ∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (ρ i)) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q))
    (he : 1 ≤ e) (hne : d * (e - 1) + 1 ≤ n)
    (hJ : J = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * ρ i) ^ e))
    (hfp : Algebra.FinitePresentation Rb Ab)
    (hqb : (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q).IsPrime)
    (hres : LocalSmoothingSituation.IsResolvableAfterLocalizing
      { R := Rb, A := Ab, Λ := Λ ⧸ J, q := Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q,
        algebraRΛ := instRbΛ, isScalarTower := tw, finitePresentation := hfp,
        isPrimeQ := hqb }) :
    @CanBeResolved Rb Ab (Λ ⧸ J) _ _ _ _ _ instRbΛ tw
      (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q) := by
  let _ := hqb
  let _ := instRbΛ
  let _ := tw
  let S : LocalSmoothingSituation.{u, u, u} :=
    { R := Rb, A := Ab, Λ := Λ ⧸ J, q := Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q,
      algebraRΛ := instRbΛ, isScalarTower := tw, finitePresentation := hfp,
      isPrimeQ := hqb }
  by_cases hle : S.radicalSingularIdealExtension ≤ Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) q
  · refine LocalSmoothingSituation.canBeResolved_of_nilpotent_generators S
      (fun i => toLocQuot q J (ρ i))
      (maximalIdeal_eq_span_toLocQuot q J hJq ρ hspan)
      (fun i => isNilpotent_toLocQuot q J hJq ρ δ hδ hJ i) ⟨⟨inferInstance, hle⟩, ?_⟩ hres
    rintro p ⟨hp, -⟩ hpq
    exact le_of_isPrime_le_map_quotient q J hJq ρ δ hδ hspan he hne hJ p hp hpq
  · exact canBeResolved_of_not_le _ hle

/-! ### The residual hypothesis: items (22)–(26) -/

/-- **Items (22)–(26) of the proof of Stacks 07FJ** — Stacks 07G6, 07G7, 07G8, 07G9 and 07GA.
This is `Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientResolvable` verbatim, on the same data, with the
conclusion weakened from `CanBeResolved` to
`Stacks.Smoothing.LocalSmoothingSituation.IsResolvableAfterLocalizing`: the twisted quotient
chain of item (18) need only be resolved after localizing at `𝔮`. The passage from this to the
unlocalized statement is item (20), proved in
`Stacks.Smoothing.canBeResolved_quotient_of_isResolvableAfterLocalizing`.

In the source, the five remaining items run: from the chain over `(R/I)_𝔯` to the chain over
`(R/JR)_𝔭` with `J = (π_1^e, …, π_d^e)` (07G6, a base change of the chain), from there to the
chain over `(R/𝔭^nR)_𝔭` (07G7, using `𝔭^n ⊆ J`), the replacement of `C` by `B` through the
retraction `C → B` (07G8), the identification `R_𝔭/𝔭^nR_𝔭 = Λ_0[t_1, …, t_d]` with
`Λ_0 = k[y_1, …, y_m]_𝔭/𝔭^n` together with the ind-smoothness of `D'[t_1, …, t_d]` over it
(07G9), and finally the twisted map `B → D'[t_1, …, t_d]`, `x_i ↦ π_i t_i`,
`z_{ij} ↦ λ_{ij}t_i^{2N}/δ_i^{2N}` (07GA). The lemmas realizing each of those five steps are
proved — `canBeResolved_of_canBeResolved_baseChange`,
`canBeResolved_quotient_of_canBeResolved`, `hasSmoothFactorization_of_algHom`,
`canBeResolved_of_factorization_mvPolynomial` and
`exists_algHom_parameterPowerAlgebra_mvPolynomial` — but the chain of localizations and
quotients joining them is not assembled here.

The two extra hypotheses `hfp` and `hqb` are the side conditions needed to state the conclusion
at all — finite presentation of the quotient chain and primality of `𝔮/IΛ`; both are discharged
where this definition is used, so carrying them only weakens the hypothesis. -/
def TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable : Prop :=
  ∀ (k A Λ : Type u) [Field k] [CommRing A] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra k A] [Algebra k Λ]
      [Algebra A Λ] [IsScalarTower k A Λ] [Algebra.FinitePresentation k A] [IsNoetherianRing Λ]
      [Algebra.IsGeometricallyRegular k Λ] (q : Ideal Λ) [q.IsPrime]
      {t d m N n c : ℕ} (a : Fin t → A)
      (C : Type u) [CommRing C] [Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) C]
      [Algebra (parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a) C]
      [Algebra.FiniteType (parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a) C]
      [Algebra.FinitePresentation (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) C]
      (grt : C →ₐ[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a)
      (φ : MvPolynomial (Fin m) k →ₐ[k] Λ)
      (gl : Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) →+* Localization.AtPrime q)
      (u : primePowerQuotient (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) n →+* primePowerQuotient q n)
      (D : Subring (primePowerQuotient q n))
      (aD : primePowerQuotient (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) n →+* D)
      (π : Fin d → MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (δ : Fin d → Λ) (lam : Fin d → Fin t → Λ)
      (D' : Type u) [CommRing D'] [IsLocalRing D'] [IsArtinianRing D']
      (cc : D →+* D') (b' : D' →+* primePowerQuotient q n),
    0 < N → 0 < c → 1 ≤ d → 1 ≤ n → N ≤ n → d * (8 * c - 1) + 1 ≤ n →
    q ∈ (Ideal.map (algebraMap A Λ) (singularIdeal k A)).radical.minimalPrimes →
    Ideal.span (Set.range a) = singularIdeal k A →
    Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)) (q ^ N) ≤
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q))
        (Ideal.map (algebraMap A Λ) (singularIdeal k A)) →
    ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) →
    (∀ y : MvPolynomial (Fin d) k, algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) C y =
      algebraMap (parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a) C
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) (parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a) y)) →
    (∀ x : parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a,
      grt (algebraMap (parameterPowerAlgebra A d N a) C x) = x) →
    Ideal.map ((algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)).comp φ.toRingHom)
        (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) = Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)) q →
    (∀ f, gl (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)
          (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q)) f)
        = algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (φ f)) →
    gl.Flat →
    (∀ y, u (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)
            (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q)))
            (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q ^ n)) y)
        = Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q)) (q ^ n))
          (gl y)) →
    D.subtype.comp aD = u →
    (∀ x : A, algebraMap Λ (primePowerQuotient q n) (algebraMap A Λ x) ∈ D) →
    ∀ (_ : IsLocalRing (primePowerQuotient (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) n))
      (_ : IsArtinianRing (primePowerQuotient (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) n))
      (_ : IsLocalRing (primePowerQuotient q n)) (_ : IsArtinianRing (primePowerQuotient q n))
      (_ : IsLocalRing D) (_ : IsArtinianRing D),
    aD.IsEssentiallySmooth → D.subtype.Flat →
    ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q)) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) →
    (∀ i, π i ∈ Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q) →
    Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)
        (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q)) (π i))
      = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.comap φ.toRingHom q)) →
    Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q) (φ (π i)))
      = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) →
    ∀ (_ : IsLocalHom cc) (_ : IsLocalHom b'),
    cc.IsEssentiallySmooth → b'.Flat → b'.comp cc = D.subtype →
    (∀ i, δ i ∈ q.primeCompl) →
    ∀ hrel : ∀ i, (δ i * φ (π i)) ^ (2 * N) = ∑ j, algebraMap A Λ (a j) * lam i j,
    (∀ i j, ∃ w : D', b' w = algebraMap Λ (primePowerQuotient q n) (lam i j)) →
    (∀ i, ∃ w : D', b' w = algebraMap Λ (primePowerQuotient q n) (δ i)) →
    (∀ i : Fin d, IsStrictlyStandard (R := MvPolynomial (Fin d) k)
      (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) C (MvPolynomial.X i) ^ c)) →
    letI : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) :=
      (twistedBaseHom π).toRingHom.toAlgebra
    letI : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) Λ :=
      (twistedBaseToTarget φ δ).toRingHom.toAlgebra
    letI : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) Λ :=
      ((algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) Λ).comp
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k))).toAlgebra
    letI : IsScalarTower (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) Λ :=
      IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
    ∀ hcompat : ∀ y : MvPolynomial (Fin d) k,
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) Λ
            (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) y) =
          improvedAlgebraToTarget N a (fun i => δ i * φ (π i)) lam hrel grt
            (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) C y),
    letI : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) Λ :=
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift
        (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k)
          (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) Λ)
        ({ toRingHom := improvedAlgebraToTarget N a (fun i => δ i * φ (π i)) lam hrel grt,
            commutes' := fun y => (hcompat y).symm } : C →ₐ[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] Λ)
        (fun _ _ => Commute.all _ _)).toRingHom.toAlgebra
    let I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k) :=
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => twistedParameter π i ^ (8 * c))
    let ID : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) :=
      Ideal.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k)
        (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C)) I
    let IΛ : Ideal Λ := Ideal.map (algebraMap
      (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) Λ) ID
    letI : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⧸ I) (Λ ⧸ IΛ) :=
      ((algebraMap ((MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) ⧸ ID)
        (Λ ⧸ IΛ)).comp (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⧸ I)
          ((MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) ⧸ ID))).toAlgebra
    letI : IsScalarTower (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⧸ I)
        ((MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) ⧸ ID) (Λ ⧸ IΛ) :=
      IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq (fun _ => rfl)
    ∀ (hfp : Algebra.FinitePresentation (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⧸ I)
        ((MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) ⧸ ID))
      (hqb : (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk IΛ) q).IsPrime),
    LocalSmoothingSituation.IsResolvableAfterLocalizing
      { R := MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⧸ I,
        A := (MvPolynomial (Fin m ⊕ Fin d) k ⊗[MvPolynomial (Fin d) k] C) ⧸ ID,
        Λ := Λ ⧸ IΛ, q := Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk IΛ) q,
        finitePresentation := hfp, isPrimeQ := hqb }

/-- **Items (19)–(26) of the proof of Stacks 07FJ from items (22)–(26).** Granting
`Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable`, the twisted quotient chain of item (18) can
be resolved, which is `Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientResolvable`. The content added here is
item (20), Stacks 07G4. -/
theorem twistedQuotientResolvable_of_locallyResolvable
    (h : TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable.{u}) : TwistedQuotientResolvable.{u} := by
  intro k A Λ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ q _ t d m N n c a C _ _ _ _ _ grt φ gl u D aD π δ lam
    D' _ _ _ cc b' hN hc hd1 hn hNn hnbound hq ha hqN hd hCalg hgrt hmapφ hgφ hgflat hu
    hDsub hAD instP1 instP2 instQ1 instQ2 instD1 instD2 hess hDflat hdimP hπmem hπspan
    hπΛspan instLHcc instLHb' hess' hflat' hcomp' hδq hrel hlamD' hδD' hstdC hcompat
    I ID IL
  have hILspan : IL = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (δ i * φ (π i)) ^ (8 * c)) :=
    map_map_span_pow_eq _ _ (twistedParameter π) δ (fun i => φ (π i))
      (fun i => mul_map_one_eq
        (improvedAlgebraToTarget N a (fun i => δ i * φ (π i)) lam hrel grt)
        (twistedBaseToTarget φ δ (twistedParameter π i))
        (twistedBaseToTarget_twistedParameter φ π δ i)) rfl rfl rfl
  have hILq : IL ≤ q :=
    span_mul_pow_le q (fun i => φ (π i)) δ (fun i => Ideal.mem_comap.mp (hπmem i))
      (show 1 ≤ 8 * c by omega) hILspan
  exact canBeResolved_quotient_of_isResolvableAfterLocalizing q IL hILq (fun i => φ (π i)) δ
    hδq hπΛspan (by omega) hnbound hILspan (finitePresentation_quotient I)
    (isPrime_map_quotient q IL hILq)
    (h k A Λ q a C grt φ gl u D aD π δ lam D' cc b' hN hc hd1 hn hNn hnbound hq ha
      hqN hd hCalg hgrt hmapφ hgφ hgflat hu hDsub hAD instP1 instP2 instQ1 instQ2 instD1
      instD2 hess hDflat hdimP hπmem hπspan hπΛspan instLHcc instLHb' hess' hflat' hcomp'
      hδq hrel hlamD' hδD' hstdC hcompat (finitePresentation_quotient I)
      (isPrime_map_quotient q IL hILq))

/-! ### The state of Stacks 07FJ -/

/-- **Stacks 07FJ from two hypotheses.** Let `k → A → Λ ⊃ 𝔮` be as in Situation 07F7 with `k` of
characteristic `p > 0`, `Λ` Noetherian and geometrically regular over `k`, and `𝔮` minimal over
`𝔥_A`. Then the chain can be resolved, granting exactly two undischarged hypotheses:

* `Stacks.Smoothing.HasArtinianApproximationData` — item (9) of the source's proof, which is
  Stacks 07FT, i.e. clauses (2) and (3) of Stacks 07FH in the generality of the tag. The lemma
  `Stacks.Smoothing.exists_mvPolynomial_localArtinianFactorization_mem` is this statement under
  the extra hypothesis that `κ(𝔮)` be essentially of finite type over `k`.
* `Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable` — items (22)–(26) of the source's proof,
  which are Stacks 07G6, 07G7, 07G8, 07G9 and 07GA.

Everything else in the twenty-six item proof is proved: items (1)–(17) in
`Stacks.Smoothing.canBeResolvedInPositiveCharacteristic_of_hasArtinianApproximationData`, items
(19)–(21) and item (20) (tag 07G4) in
`Stacks.Smoothing.twistedQuotientResolvable_of_locallyResolvable`. This theorem is the
composition of those two, and it is what makes the true dependency of 07FJ visible: the second
hypothesis is `TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable`, not the stronger
`Stacks.Smoothing.TwistedQuotientResolvable`.

No `@[stacks 07FJ]` attribute is attached: a statement conditional on hypotheses is not a
formalization of the tag. Both are proved downstream, in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Smoothing/TwistedQuotientClosure.lean`, which is where the attribute
sits, on `Stacks.Smoothing.canBeResolvedInPositiveCharacteristic`. -/
theorem canBeResolvedInPositiveCharacteristic_of_locallyResolvable
    (h07FT : HasArtinianApproximationData.{u})
    (hloc : TwistedQuotientLocallyResolvable.{u}) :
    CanBeResolvedInPositiveCharacteristic.{u} :=
  canBeResolvedInPositiveCharacteristic_of_hasArtinianApproximationData h07FT
    (twistedQuotientResolvable_of_locallyResolvable hloc)

end Stacks.Smoothing

